From 8c6ba7f94327714ac36ea29c625dfe8c7f9520a3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stew Forster <stew675@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 12:17:51 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 24/28] WIP HC16: scope the BF16 activation state per backend
 context

The HC16 F32-elision keeps each producer's BF16 activation copy in a
file-scope cache/slot set and the "BF16-only" marks in file-scope sets
(ggml/src/ggml-cuda/mmb.cu).  Both were shared by every CUDA backend
context in the process, so the MTP target and its draft head (two
llama_contexts with separate schedulers) corrupted each other:

  - the draft's ggml_cuda_mmb_begin_graph() freed the target's cache
    buffers at the start of every draft compute, so a target producer that
    had elided its F32 output left its consumer reading a never-written
    buffer once the cache entry was gone;
  - the marks leaked across contexts, so a context could elide a producer
    based on another context's marks.

The symptom was nondeterministic greedy text under MTP at depth (128K MTP
n_max 1 gave five different hashes in five runs; the 40K draft diverged
from plain), while GGML_CUDA_MMB_HC16=0 was deterministic and pure.

Fix:
  * move the whole MMB BF16 state (per-graph activation cache, pinned
    producer slots, BF16-only/copy marks and their lifetime) into a
    per-backend-context mmb_ctx_state selected by an "active context"
    pointer set at the start of ggml_backend_cuda_graph_optimize and
    _graph_compute;
  * rebuild the marks per graph with an explicit per-context
    after-compute / first-node lifetime (ggml_cuda_mmb_optimize_begin and
    _compute_done) instead of the global key hack;
  * the step-3 marking pass now classifies a producer's consumers over the
    whole scheduled graph (new ggml_backend_graph_optimize_params.full_graph)
    and refuses to elide a tensor that has a consumer in another split --
    the per-compute activation cache does not span splits.

Gates (gfx1151, qwen4exp IQ4_NL + Q4_K_M MTP sidecar, f16 KV):
  - 128K MTP n_max 1: 5 runs, one hash == plain == HC16=0 (770e770ae7d6);
  - 40K: plain == dense n1/n3 == sparse n1/n3/n5 (8285d12d40ca),
    deterministic over repeats;
  - 8192 plain == dense == sparse (3553e76d3a9e); width probe PASS;
  - llama-imatrix NanBeige4.2-3B-BF16 clean, imatrix file byte-identical
    to HC16=0; FLASH_ATTN_QSA 2/2, GATED_DELTA_NET 2/2;
  - 40K -n 200 n_max 3: plain 28.4 t/s, dense MTP 33.4 t/s (HC16 on and
    off identical), so HC16 is preserved under MTP.
